<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K'an Joy Chitam II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">644–c. 721</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">K'an Joy Chitam II was king of the Maya city of Palenque from 702, a son of K'inich Janaab' <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal">Pakal</a>. In 711 he was captured by the rival city of Toniná, which depicted him bound as a prisoner on a relief. He seems to have survived and returned, but Palenque declined through the eighth century.</p></div>
